---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import authorPhoto from '../assets/denis-ethier.png';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead 
			title="Our Mission: The Human Glue Between Patients & Doctors | Decoding The Burn" 
			description="Bridging the communication and diagnostic gap between Burning Mouth Syndrome sufferers, dentists, physicians, and clinical researchers." 
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<!-- Hero Section Following Homepage Model -->
			<section class="hero-centered-wrapper">
				<div class="hero-centered-header">
					<MedicalDisclaimer />
					<h1 class="hero-centered-title">
						The Human Glue: Bridging Patients &amp;&nbsp;Doctors
					</h1>
					<p class="hero-centered-subtitle">
						We connect lived patient time-series data with clinical neuroscience to bridge the communication chasm.
						Here is why uniting sufferers, dentists, and physicians is the key to lasting&nbsp;relief.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Video on Top -->
				<div class="hero-video-centered">
					<div class="video-placeholder-wrapper" style="cursor: default;">
						<Image 
							src={authorPhoto} 
							alt="Denis Ethier - Our Mission and Bridge" 
							class="video-placeholder-img" 
							width={1400} 
							height={788}
						/>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Story Card Under Video -->
				<article class="personal-story-section">
					<h2 class="story-heading">My Story &amp; Why We Need the Human&nbsp;Glue</h2>
					<div class="story-lead">
						<p>
							After consulting five dentists and five medical doctors with severe 10/10 oral pain, I witnessed firsthand the communication chasm in modern medicine. When you are in agony, you need urgency. But busy clinicians with 15-minute appointment slots must maintain detachment, often writing 'idiopathic discomfort with anxiety' in charts when you feel like your mouth is on&nbsp;fire.
						</p>
						<p>
							I realized that doctors aren't malicious, they simply lack the tools and time to capture dense time-series data. The mission of Decoding The Burn is to serve as the human glue: translating lived patient observations into objective clinical terms so patients and clinicians can solve this mystery&nbsp;together.
						</p>
						<p class="continue-reading-p">
							<a href="/podcast" class="continue-reading-link">Listen to the latest podcast discussions &rarr;</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			</section>

			<div class="mission-content-container">
				<!-- 1. The Core Problem: The Communication Chasm -->
				<section class="mission-section">
					<div class="problem-card">
						<h2 class="section-title">The Communication Chasm in Modern Medicine</h2>
						<p class="section-lead">
							When you walk into a specialist clinic with severe 10/10 oral burning, your life is in crisis. Every meal is a battle with fire, and you cannot sleep. But for the busy clinician seeing dozens of complex patients a day, they must maintain emotional detachment to manage clinical volume. As a result, acute patient agony often gets translated into standardized, sanitized medical&nbsp;jargon:
						</p>
						<div class="quote-contrast-grid">
							<div class="contrast-box patient-side">
								<span class="box-label label-red">What the Patient Experiences</span>
								<p class="quote-text">"My mouth is on fire 24/7. When I drink coffee or eat an orange, the burning shoots to a blinding 10/10. I can't concentrate on my job or sleep at night."</p>
							</div>
							<div class="contrast-box chart-side">
								<span class="box-label label-blue">What Gets Written in the Chart</span>
								<p class="quote-text">"Oral mucosa appears unremarkable. Mild-to-moderate neuropathic discomfort (3-5/10) with anxious overlay. Etiology idiopathic. Reassure patient."</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<p class="section-foot">
							When patients request their medical records and see their 10/10 agony reduced to a <em>"mild 3/10 with anxiety"</em>, they choke. They feel gaslighted, insulted, and abandoned. Many give up entirely. This is where the podcast steps&nbsp;in.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- 2. The Human Glue Diagram & Architecture -->
				<section class="mission-section">
					<h2 class="section-title text-center">How The Podcast Acts as the Human Glue</h2>
					<p class="section-lead text-center">
						We don't assign blame or attack doctors. We translate the two worlds so both sides can collaborate on real biological&nbsp;solutions.
					</p>

					<div class="glue-diagram-container">
						<div class="diagram-hub">
							<span class="hub-label">The Podcast &amp; Research Hub</span>
							<h3 class="hub-title">Decoding The Burn &bull; The BMS Podcast</h3>
							<p class="hub-motto">"The Rosetta Stone Between Lived Agony &amp; Clinical Science"</p>
						</div>

						<div class="diagram-branches">
							<!-- Branch 1: For Patients -->
							<div class="branch-card branch-patient">
								<div class="branch-header">
									<span class="branch-icon" aria-hidden="true">🛡️</span>
									<h4 class="branch-title">For Patients &amp; Sufferers</h4>
								</div>
								<ul class="branch-list">
									<li><strong>Decodes Medical Jargon:</strong> Explains why doctors write "3/10" or "anxious" so patients don't panic, take it personally, or despair.</li>
									<li><strong>Biophysical Validation:</strong> Demonstrates that your burning has physical ion-channel and hardware mechanisms, not "imagined stress."</li>
									<li><strong>Constructive Communication:</strong> Teaches patients how to speak with dentists and doctors with clear, structured time-series logs.</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<!-- Branch 2: For Clinicians -->
							<div class="branch-card branch-clinician">
								<div class="branch-header">
									<span class="branch-icon" aria-hidden="true">🩺</span>
									<h4 class="branch-title">For Clinicians &amp; Researchers</h4>
								</div>
								<ul class="branch-list">
									<li><strong>The High-Functioning 10/10:</strong> Explains why stoic, articulate patients are still in excruciating pain despite not screaming in the chair.</li>
									<li><strong>Hardware &amp; Acid Mechanics:</strong> Shares high-resolution data on subgingival crown leaks, exposed dentin tubules, and dietary acid triggers.</li>
									<li><strong>Beyond "Luck" &amp; Placebo:</strong> Proves that dietary elimination remission is reproducible biophysics and biochemistry, not a fluke.</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- 3. Our Three Core Pillars -->
				<section class="mission-section">
					<h2 class="section-title">The Three Pillars of Our Mission</h2>
					<div class="pillars-grid">
						<div class="pillar-card">
							<span class="pillar-num">01</span>
							<h3 class="pillar-heading">Radical Data Transparency</h3>
							<p class="pillar-desc">
								We share every radiograph, symptom log, dietary protocol, and dental record publicly. By putting real N=1 data in the open, we eliminate guesswork and give researchers a tangible baseline to&nbsp;study.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="pillar-card">
							<span class="pillar-num">02</span>
							<h3 class="pillar-heading">Root-Cause Engineering</h3>
							<p class="pillar-desc">
								We treat the human mouth like a high-precision electrical and biochemical system. When a nerve fires distress, we don't just sedate the brain with pharmaceuticals; we track down the physical trigger causing the&nbsp;leak.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="pillar-card">
							<span class="pillar-num">03</span>
							<h3 class="pillar-heading">Collaborative Problem-Solving</h3>
							<p class="pillar-desc">
								We invite dentists, oral medicine specialists, neurologists, and academic researchers to brainstorm openly on air without the fear of needing perfect textbook answers. Real discoveries happen through open&nbsp;dialogue.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- CTA Box -->
				<section class="mission-cta-box">
					<h2 class="cta-title">Be Part of the Solution</h2>
					<p class="cta-subtitle">
						Whether you are enduring BMS, practicing dentistry, or researching neuropathic pain, your voice and data can help solve this puzzle for&nbsp;millions.
					</p>
					<div class="cta-actions">
						<a href="/podcast#apply" class="btn btn-primary cta-btn">Apply to Be a Guest &rarr;</a>
						<a href="/blog/how-i-solved-my-burning-mouth-syndrome/" class="btn btn-outline cta-btn">Read Post #1: My Journey</a>
					</div>
				</section>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />

		<style>
			.mission-content-container {
				max-width: 1080px;
				margin: 1rem auto 5rem;
				padding: 0 1.5rem;
			}

			.mission-section {
				margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
			}

			.section-title {
				font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem);
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			}

			.section-lead {
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
				color: #334155;
				margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
				text-wrap: pretty;
			}

			.text-center {
				text-align: center;
			}

			.problem-card {
				background: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
				border-radius: 24px;
				padding: 2.75rem 2.5rem;
				box-shadow: 0 4px 20px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
			}

			.quote-contrast-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.5rem;
				margin: 2rem 0;
			}

			.contrast-box {
				border-radius: 16px;
				padding: 1.75rem;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
			}

			.patient-side {
				background: #fff1f2;
				border: 1px solid #fecdd3;
			}

			.chart-side {
				background: #eff6ff;
				border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
			}

			.box-label {
				align-self: flex-start;
				font-size: 0.92rem;
				font-weight: 700;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
			}

			.label-red {
				color: #be123c;
			}

			.label-blue {
				color: #1d4ed8;
			}

			.quote-text {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				color: #1e293b;
				font-style: italic;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.section-foot {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
				color: #475569;
				margin: 0;
				text-wrap: pretty;
			}

			/* Glue Diagram Styling */
			.glue-diagram-container {
				background: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
				border-radius: 24px;
				padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
				margin-top: 2rem;
				box-shadow: 0 10px 30px -5px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
			}

			.diagram-hub {
				background: #0f172a;
				border-radius: 18px;
				padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
				text-align: center;
				color: #ffffff;
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
				box-shadow: 0 8px 24px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.2);
			}

			.hub-label {
				display: block;
				font-size: 0.88rem;
				font-weight: 700;
				color: #a78bfa;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.hub-title {
				font-size: 1.65rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #ffffff;
				margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;
			}

			.hub-motto {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				color: #cbd5e1;
				font-style: italic;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.diagram-branches {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.75rem;
			}

			.branch-card {
				background: #f8fafc;
				border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
				border-radius: 18px;
				padding: 2rem;
			}

			.branch-header {
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.75rem;
				margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
				padding-bottom: 0.85rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
			}

			.branch-icon {
				font-size: 1.6rem;
			}

			.branch-title {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.branch-list {
				margin: 0;
				padding-left: 1.25rem;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				gap: 0.85rem;
				color: #334155;
				font-size: 0.98rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			/* Pillars Styling */
			.pillars-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
				margin-top: 2rem;
			}

			.pillar-card {
				background: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
				border-radius: 20px;
				padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
				box-shadow: 0 4px 16px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
			}

			.pillar-num {
				display: block;
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: #c8382c;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
			}

			.pillar-heading {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
			}

			.pillar-desc {
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				color: #475569;
				margin: 0;
				text-wrap: pretty;
			}

			/* CTA Box */
			.mission-cta-box {
				background: #fdfbf7;
				border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
				border-radius: 24px;
				padding: 3.5rem 2.5rem;
				text-align: center;
				margin-bottom: 5rem;
			}

			.cta-title {
				font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.3rem);
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
			}

			.cta-subtitle {
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				color: #475569;
				max-width: 650px;
				margin: 0 auto 2rem auto;
				text-wrap: balance;
			}

			.cta-actions {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				gap: 1.25rem;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
			}

			.cta-btn {
				padding: 0.95rem 2.25rem;
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
